(:id "port/python/packet/unions" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_unions_test.go: TestPythonPacketUnions" "make packet-void-python (make/python-packet-unions.mk)" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_unions_test.go: TestPythonPacketUnionsNegativeControl" "make packet-void-python-negative-control (make/python-packet-unions.mk)") :tested-revision "d0601d0e31c9e1965a4cc80c862ca1e068289e12" :note "2026-11-15: tagged unions of type payloads held to the generated Go packet code on the test's own fixture schema: the union alone (Action, payload arms between payload-free ones, a 3-bit tag with 6 and 7 unused) and beside the core's kinds (an enum, flags, full-width integers and a bool in the payloads, a union inside a type and inside another union's payload, both inside Envelope between other fields). Python writes the 17 cases' bytes exactly as Go writes them, reads them back to an equal value that writes back byte-identical, leaves every unselected arm at its declared defaults, and gives each of Go's read verdicts its own: the unused tags, empty and trailing input, and every case one byte short and one byte long, all refused. The leg's half of test/packet-void reads and writes its hand-calculated SPEC section 4.8 wire byte for byte. Out-of-contract writes raise InvalidValue naming the field path. The controls plant one extra set bit on a payload-free arm's write, and a tag range that admits the unused tags on a read, each in a copy of the generated code, and each probe goes red by name. Run on macOS arm64 under CPython 3.11.18 (floor) and 3.15.2 (current) from make dist-python, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, mypy 1.18.2 --strict --python-version 3.11 over each generated tree, at this revision; no wire golden is claimed here.")
(:id "port/python/packet/payload-free-arms" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/python/python_packet_unions_test.go: TestPythonPacketUnions" "make packet-void-python (make/python-packet-unions.mk)" "internal/codegen/python/python_packet_unions_test.go: TestPythonPacketUnionsNegativeControl" "make packet-void-python-negative-control (make/python-packet-unions.mk)") :tested-revision "d0601d0e31c9e1965a4cc80c862ca1e068289e12" :note "2026-11-15: every named payload-free arm spends exactly its tag bits. In the leg's half of test/packet-void, Mixed None/Ping/Pong and Tags None/Pong write and read 0x00, 0x01, 0x03 and 0x02, Single Ack 0x01 in one bit, Empty None writes no bits, and Frame puts a payload-free tag between two one-bit bools as 0x0B; Tags' unused tag 3 and a set bit past a tag are refused. Against the generated Go packet code, the payload-free arms Stop, Halt, Pause and Idle, alone and nested, write Go's bytes and read back equal with every payload arm at its declared defaults. The controls plant one extra set bit on a payload-free arm's write, and a tag range over the unused tags on a read, in a copy of the generated code, and each goes red by name. Run on macOS arm64 under CPython 3.11.18 and 3.15.2 from make dist-python, SCHEMA_SLOW=1, with mypy --strict over each generated tree, at this revision; no wire golden is claimed here.")
